# Major Mono Display Font - Lowercase Rule

**CRITICAL RULE**: The "Major Mono Display Regular" font must ALWAYS display text in lowercase, regardless of the input case.

## Implementation Requirements:

1. **NEVER use** `.font(.custom("Major Mono Display Regular", size: X))` directly on Text views
2. **ALWAYS use** one of these methods instead:
   - `.majorMonoFont(size: X)` modifier (preferred for existing Text views)
   - `Text.majorMono(content, size: X)` static method (for new Text views)

## Examples:

❌ **WRONG**:
```swift
Text(project.name)
    .font(.custom("Major Mono Display Regular", size: 17))
    .textCase(nil)
```

✅ **CORRECT**:
```swift
Text(project.name)
    .majorMonoFont(size: 17)
```

Or:
```swift
Text.majorMono(project.name, size: 17)
```

## Why:
The Major Mono Display font should never display uppercase letters. The `.majorMonoFont()` modifier and `Text.majorMono()` helper automatically enforce lowercase display using `.textCase(.lowercase)`, ensuring consistent lowercase rendering regardless of user input or data source.

## When reviewing or writing code:
- If you see `.font(.custom("Major Mono Display Regular"` anywhere, replace it with `.majorMonoFont(size: X)`
- Remove any `.textCase(nil)` that was used with this font
- Ensure all text using this font displays in lowercase

